9, 2.050, 2.045, 2.022} ms/x — asymptotes at per-x Lucy DP cost. CORRELATED (consecutive integers, w=M): T_amort ∈ {2.700, 0.693, 0.182, 0.071} ms/x — scales as T_anchor/M + O(M/log M). **33× gap at M=64** between uncorrelated and correlated. CORRELATED-LOG² (w = log²x = 190, M = 64): 0.134 ms/x, still 15× faster than uncorrelated. **What dichotomy ENABLES**: for correlated narrow-window D (width = polylog², M ≥ T_anchor/polylog), T_per_x_amort = polylog. **CONDITIONAL batch-polylog π(x) algorithm exists for correlated batches in polylog windows** — exactly the C4 hybrid (S120 Aggarwal × Dusart × BPSW) reframed as a batch-polylog result. **What dichotomy RULES OUT**: Aggarwal binary-search request pattern has midpoints factor-2 apart, far outside polylog window; falls on uncorrelated side. UNCONDITIONAL negative result: no algorithm in {explicit-formula, HKM, Aggarwal} achieves batch-polylog over uncorrelated batched queries. **Three-pillar lower bound** (combining slots 1-4): T_per_x_amort(uncorrelated, M = poly log x_max) ≥ Θ̃(x^{1/2}) under Montgomery, Θ(x^{2/3}/log²) unconditional. Lower bound TIGHT under Galway 2004 / LMO 1985 / Aggarwal 2025. **Five-session arc summary**: slot 1 (T_eval=Θ(K) asymptotically), slot 2 (Schönhage multipoint constant-factor), slot 3 (HKM trivial sieve only), slot 4 (Aggarwal log₂(n)×Lucy(R0)), slot 5 (DICHOTOMY + cross-NTT + C4 reframe). **Thread 5 closes 5_final at S224.** S202 WRAP "legitimate falsifier of Thread 3" (cross-x amortisation) is now resolved: the per-pillar α_p lower bounds combined with the dichotomy preclude batch-polylog for unrestricted batched-query regime. **Falsifiers (open after Thread 5 closure)**: (1) non-Lucy / non-HKM combinatorial π(x) breaking Θ(x^{2/3}) per-query — none in 40+ years; (2) Aggarwal variant with fewer than log₂(n) π-queries — info-theoretically tight; (3) per-query primitive polylog-cost on uncorrelated x_i — would break Thread 3 directly; (4) correlation primitive defeating polylog-window restriction — Schönhage cluster-width bound (slot 2) provides the structural ceiling. **Cross-domain ingredient**: amortised algorithmics (Tarjan 1985 / Iacono 2008 / Demaine-Patrascu 2008): USED I (final). Slot 5 completes the application — the dichotomy with explicit per-pillar constants. Information-theoretic batched lower bounds (Demaine-Patrascu 2008): PROPOSED → USED PARTIAL — first application to π(x) in this project. Cites E1.5 (per-query bit-content barrier — realised structurally at batch level via I(D;π)), E3.1 (Connes — slot-1 setup matches Hiary), E6.6 (Aggarwal — placed on uncorrelated side), E6.7 (Deleglise-Rivat — α_HKM is exactly E6.7 amortisation-stable), E6.8 (Dusart bracket — source of slot-4 hyperbola-density mismatch), S120 (C4 reframed as conditional batch-polylog), S190 / S202 / S215 (Threads 1-4 closures extended to batched-query frontier), S217 (Aggarwal-on-π_tilde cross-checked at slot 4), S220-S223 (slots 1-4 unified). **Thread 5 closure plus Threads 1-4 = ALL FIVE CLAUDE.md "Highest-EV mathematical threads" CLOSED**; per CLAUDE.md instruction, next commit-mode invocation should escalate to user for next-thread selection (frontier_gen, Lean formalisation arc, or publication synthesis). See `experiments/analytic/cross_x_amortisation/{cross_x_dichotomy_wrap.py, cross_x_dichotomy_wrap_results.md, cross_x_dichotomy.csv, cross_x_lowerbound.csv}`, `archive/sessions/session224_commit_cross_x_amortisation.md`. | 224 |
