e HL imprint and SL_2(Z) Möbius action on Q (which changes denominators non-multiplicatively) are categorically incompatible; chi_P does NOT carry quantum-modular structure for any weight k or any SL_2(Z) generator with c ≠ 0. **Adds EDGE E7.22** (negative-shape) — first identification of HL/SL_2(Z) structural incompatibility. **A-grade ruled out**: no quantum-modular polylog primality witness exists from rational evaluation of f_N. **Successor B-grade target identified**: Eichler integral of half-integer-weight pseudo-modular form with prime-supported Fourier coefficients (Bringmann-Folsom-Ono-Rhoades 2017 §21.3) — does the lift to upper half-plane H carry quantum-modular structure that rational evaluation misses? **Cross-domain ingredient**: Zagier 2010 quantum modular forms (Clay Math. Proc. 11) — UNUSED before; CROSS_DOMAIN_TECHNIQUES.md §6 row PROPOSED → USED I (E7.22). Cites E2.21 (S138, HL imprint at L^∞), E2.20 (S134, Mahler), E2.13 (Gowers U^k), E1.5 (explicit formula), E7.21 (S197, natural boundary). See `experiments/analytic/d37_quantum_modular_chi_p/{d37_quantum_modular_chi_p.py, d37_quantum_modular_chi_p_results.md, summary_N*.json, rows_k*_N*.json}`, `archive/sessions/session225_d37_quantum_modular_chi_p.md`. | 225 |
